### Flow 1: Q&A - course question
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Tell me about your data courses, what do you have?",
  "session_id": "qa-demo"
}

### Flow 1: Q&A - follow-up, same session
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Do you have anything on design?",
  "session_id": "qa-demo"
}

### Flow 1b: Semantic RAG - no keyword overlap (expects: Python Foundations)
# "never written a line of code" -> matches "starts from absolute zero / no prior
# programming experience", even though the query never says "beginner" or "Python".
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "I have never written a line of code in my life, where do I start?",
  "session_id": "rag-demo"
}

### Flow 1b: Semantic RAG - intent, not keywords (expects: Confident Public Speaking)
# "terrified of presenting" -> matches "for people who dread presenting / nerves".
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "I get terrified whenever I have to present to a room",
  "session_id": "rag-demo"
}

### Flow 1b: Semantic RAG - paraphrase (expects: Data Analysis with Pandas)
# "messy spreadsheets into something meaningful" -> matches the description directly.
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "How do I turn messy spreadsheets into something meaningful?",
  "session_id": "rag-demo"
}

### Flow 1b: Semantic RAG - problem statement (expects: DevOps and CI/CD Pipelines)
# "deployments keep breaking on Fridays" -> matches "teams tired of manual
# deployments breaking on Friday afternoons", zero shared technical keywords.
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Our releases keep breaking every time we ship, it is all manual",
  "session_id": "rag-demo"
}

### Flow 1b: Semantic RAG - career goal (expects: Product Management Foundations)
# "moving from engineering into deciding what to build".
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "I am an engineer who wants to move into deciding what we build",
  "session_id": "rag-demo"
}

### Flow 2: Enroll - HITL step 1: draft
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "I want to enroll in Python Foundations",
  "session_id": "enroll-demo"
}

### Flow 2: Enroll - HITL step 2: confirm
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "yes",
  "session_id": "enroll-demo"
}

### Flow 2 (variant): Enroll - HITL step 1: draft
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Sign me up for UX Design Fundamentals",
  "session_id": "enroll-cancel-demo"
}

### Flow 2 (variant): Enroll - HITL step 2: cancel
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "no",
  "session_id": "enroll-cancel-demo"
}

### Router fix: enrollment management must NOT route to track
# These read like status questions but are management intent -> expects the enroll path.
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "I want to cancel my enrollment",
  "session_id": "router-fix-demo"
}

### Router fix: refund request -> enroll path, not track
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "I am not happy with the course, I want a refund",
  "session_id": "router-fix-demo-2"
}

### Guardrail: off-topic - should be rejected
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "What's the weather like today?",
  "session_id": "guard-demo"
}

### Guardrail: empty message - Pydantic 422
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "",
  "session_id": "guard-demo"
}

### Flow 3: Check enrollment status (needs a confirmed enrollment first)
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "What is the status of my enrollments?",
  "session_id": "enroll-demo"
}

### Flow 3: Check progress - no enrollments yet
POST {{host}}/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "How far along am I in my course?",
  "session_id": "track-new"
}
